From 4574041408c9a16f8ead5635ba3fa358e97f0a37 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 22:46:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02448/11362] [outer-loop] bridge v2: richer value head ROUTES
 a reachable floor win (cn04 unlocked)

Operator: take on the richer-value/TRM lever. First a DIAGNOSTIC settled which component
to build: for the 6 gap-1 floor games, the oracle's winning actions are 91-100% present
in the live explorer's candidate set -> the wins are REACHABLE; the failure is ROUTING,
not action-generation. So a value head that orders the search CAN help (the lever is real).

Built cross_game_features_v2 (frame-only): the 5 v1 scalars + a 6x6 spatial occupancy map
(41 features) so the head can locate WHERE activity is, not just how much (v1 threw away
all spatial structure -> inert at routing). Trained on the same 480-state, 16-game,
frame-only, steps-to-next-level-up corpus.

A/B (graph_explore_solve_v2 A*-routed: depth + 5*value) on the 6 floor games:
  cn04:  BFS L0, v1 L0, v2 L1 SOLVED   <- the richer head ROUTED a win neither BFS nor v1 found
  sk48:  all solve (reachable by BFS at this budget)
  ar25/ka59/sc25/wa30: still L0 (v2 did not help those)
-> v2 unlocked 1/6 floor games over BFS. NOT a silver bullet, but a REAL positive: the
   flywheel produces value, and richer features matter (v1's 5 scalars did not unlock cn04).

This is measured on graph_explore_solve_v2's A* heuristic slot, NOT yet the live
StepwiseExplorer (whose depth-primary tiebreak is too weak -- A* depth+weight*value is what
routed cn04). NEXT: port A* value-routing into the live explorer + re-run the live oracle-gap
eval to see whether cn04 (gap-1) and others close in the actual submitted agent (8/32 -> ?).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
